# Fake News Detection

A Streamlit application that classifies news text as real or fake using a locally
fine-tuned XLM-RoBERTa model. It supports direct text input and extracting text
from a URL.

## Run the application

1. Install Python 3 and the dependencies:

   ```powershell
   py -m venv .venv
   .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
   python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

2. Copy the trained `fake_news_model` directory into the project root, next to
   `model_loader.py`.
3. Start Streamlit:

   ```powershell
   python -m streamlit run app.py
   ```

The model loader reports an error when the local model directory is missing.
The model and training datasets are intentionally excluded from Git because
they are very large; keep the model in the project root and the datasets under
`data/`, or store them in a model/dataset hosting service. Training scripts and
code are included in this repository.
